{
  "text": "The caller passes items and a requested locale. The renderer selects a layout first. That helper returns the resolved locale and labels. Next, the renderer derives the summary. The helper validates every quantity, then builds the rows and total. Those values return to the renderer. The renderer passes rows and labels to the table helper. Item names are escaped before insertion. The helper returns the completed HTML table. Finally, the renderer returns locale, title, total, and body. For valid inputs, this result matches the original implementation. With French Canadian requested, the layout helper extracts French. It tries the full locale, then French, then English. French is the first available layout. The renderer next calls the summary helper. A negative quantity fails validation. The helper throws a range error before calculating rows or a total. There is no catch in the renderer. The error propagates to the caller, and table rendering never runs. This rejection is a behavior change from the original implementation.",
